refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
truesnmp_set_enum_print boolenable
This function toggles whether snmpwalk/snmpget etc. return enum values as the raw integer or together with their label from the MIB. It has no effect with SNMP_VALUE_PLAIN.

&reftitle.parameters;
enable
When &true;, enum values are returned as the raw integer, for example INTEGER: 1. When &false;, they are returned with their label, for example INTEGER: forwarding(1). Any scalar value is coerced to a bool.

  &reftitle.examples;

   Using snmp_set_enum_print


<?php
 snmp_set_enum_print(0);
 echo snmpget('localhost', 'public', 'IF-MIB::ifOperStatus.3') . "\n";
 snmp_set_enum_print(1);
 echo snmpget('localhost', 'public', 'IF-MIB::ifOperStatus.3') . "\n";
?>




   The above  would return

 INTEGER: up(1)
 INTEGER: 1
